e victim taking place  across the country  what more can you tell us about them  uh there are demonstrations in about uh  ten large cities in france and they  include paris  bordeaux  and there's an outrage in the country  that is comparable to the outrage when  the cartoonist of charlie abdul were  slain five years ago that  the teacher who's trying his best to  educate  children he was actually just killed by  terror  a terrorist is there any new information  about the attacker  we know quite a few things now we know  that he's an  18 year he was an 18 year old chechen  who uh  was born in moscow was refused asylum in  poland  was about to be refused asylum in france  but  that was overruled by a judge and  who apparently has been radicalized  in various ways we do not know what we  do not know is whether he was preparing  for this against this teacher it  could not have been a very long time  because the teacher had not been  targeted until  he made that course that lesson uh less  than a week ago  uh but we also know that uh  he was not a pupil in that school  he did not attend that the class he took  it upon himself  to go and kill the teacher as surely you  know  france's long-balanced secular and  christian  traditions and yet over the years  there's been a rise in  influx some would say of extremist  elements  outsiders might quickly attribute these  attacks to that inevitable tension  how did the french explain it  the french explain it exactly as you did  which is that  uh we have had for a long time  are muslims in france because france had  muslim colonies and then  uh after colonization uh they still came  to france  and the relationships uh with the the  first generation were pretty good and  they were not radicalized in a way that  we are now seeing  which dates back from the 1980s when  wahhabi islam  extremist islam funded at the time by  saudi arabia  and now still funded by qatar and others  started  demanding more and more separate ways of  livin